.SH "NAME"
pcre2_substring_copy_bynumber \- extract numbered substring into given buffer
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_substring_copy_bynumber\fP\f(CR(pcre2_match_data *\fP\f(CImatch_data\fP\f(CR,
                                  uint32_t\fP \f(CIstringnumber\fP\f(CR,
                                  PCRE2_UCHAR *\fP\f(CIbuffer\fP\f(CR,
                                  PCRE2_SIZE *\fP\f(CIsizeptr\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This is a convenience function for extracting a captured substring into a given
buffer. The arguments are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 13
\f(CImatch_data\fP
.ad l
The match data block for the match
.TP 13
\f(CIstringnumber\fP
.ad l
Number of the required substring
.TP 13
\f(CIbuffer\fP
.ad l
Buffer to receive the string
.TP 13
\f(CIsizeptr\fP
.ad l
Length of buffer
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The \f(CIsizeptr\fP variable is updated with the length of the extracted string,
excluding the terminating zero. The yield of the function is zero for success
or one of the following error numbers:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING\fP
.ad l
there are no groups of that number
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE\fP
.ad l
the ovector was too small for that group
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_UNSET\fP
.ad l
the group did not participate in the match
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY\fP
.ad l
the buffer is too small
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.